  "id": "Compound::DB00509 - Gene::353189",
  "verbalization": "Dextrothyroxine is implicated in the pathogenesis of multiple conditions through its interaction with Liotrix, which binds to Slco4c1. The evidence suggests that Dextrothyroxine causes physiological effects such as fluid loss, cerebral artery embolism, and craniosynostosis, all of which are mediated by Liotrix. These effects are linked to Slco4c1 through the binding interaction between Liotrix and the transporter. The recurring pattern of Liotrix as a mediator between Dextrothyroxine and Slco4c1 indicates a potential mechanism where Dextrothyroxine influences the expression or activity of Slco4c1 via Liotrix. The shared lowest common ancestors, Thyroid Agent and Phenylalanine Derivative, further suggest a broader biological context in which Dextrothyroxine and Liotrix play a role. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible functional relationship where Dextrothyroxine indirectly affects Slco4c1 through Liotrix, emphasizing the role of Liotrix as a critical intermediary in this relationship.",
